Step 1: Log in to MySQL

Open the command line (Command Prompt in Windows or Terminal in macOS/Linux) and
log in to MySQL using the root user or another user with the necessary privileges:
    mysql -u root -p
You will be prompted to enter your password.

Step 2: Run the raahi.sql Script
This script will create the database and tables. After logging into the MySQL prompt,
use the following command to execute the raahi.sql file. Note: You must replace
/path/to/your/DBproject/raahi.sql with the absolute path to the file on your system.

    SOURCE /path/to/your/DBproject/raahi.sql;

Step 3: Run the tests.sql Script
After the database and tables have been successfully created, you can insert the initial data.
To do this, run the tests.sql script:
    SOURCE /path/to/your/DBproject/tests.sql;
As in the previous step, replace the placeholder with the full path to your tests.sql file.


Step 4: Verify the Setup

After successfully running both scripts, you can verify that the database,
tables, and data have been created correctly with the following commands:

Select the database:
    USE raahi_db;
Show the tables:
    SHOW TABLES;
View data from a table (e.g., Users):
    SELECT * FROM Users LIMIT 10;
By following these steps, your raahi_db database will be set up with all the necessary
tables and initial data to run your project.